WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.600
With its small town setting&nbsp;
and fresh-faced young lead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.720
DC's "Stargirl" is probably the sweetest&nbsp;
superhero show ever made — which is why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.840
her dark history of murdered family members,&nbsp;
older boyfriends and more might surprise you.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:20.080
Since she was first introduced as the new "Star&nbsp;
Spangled Kid" in 1999's "Stars and S.T.R.I.P.E.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.800
#0," Courtney Whitmore has been treated with&nbsp;
great affection by her comic book creators.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.640
This is due to the fact that her writer&nbsp;
Geoff Johns based Courtney's personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:34.000
appearance and name after his sister Courtney&nbsp;
Johns. In several interviews about Stargirl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.240
Johns spoke of the real-life Courtney's, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.800
"spirit and optimistic energy that I wanted&nbsp;
to put back in the world with Stargirl."

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.000
Tragically, Courtney Johns died in the TWA Flight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.040
800 disaster of 1996. Her comic book counterpart&nbsp;
became a tribute to her real-world inspiration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.120
and Courtney Johns was even memorialized&nbsp;
in the pilot episode of "Stargirl" by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.080
placing an edited image of her in a photo&nbsp;
alongside "Stargirl" actress Brec Bassinger.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.480
In the "Stargirl" TV show, Pat Dugan, played by&nbsp;
Luke Wilson, is Courtney Whitmore's stepfather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.920
and the former sidekick to the superhero Starman,&nbsp;
played by Joel McHale. Together, the two fought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:17.200
crime in the early twenty-first century before&nbsp;
Starman was killed and Dugan semi-retired.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.760
In the comics, Dugan served as the sidekick&nbsp;
"Stripesy" to the Star-Spangled Kid during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.000
World War II. The pair eventually joined&nbsp;
The Seven Soldiers of Victory, who were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.400
scattered throughout time after a battle&nbsp;
with Nebula-Man. Dugan wound up in Ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.640
Egypt where he was enslaved and forced&nbsp;
to work on the pyramids until members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.800
of the Justice League of America rescued&nbsp;
him and brought him back to the present.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.760
Dugan eventually found love with Courtney's mother&nbsp;
Barbara and took on the mantle of the armored hero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.880
S.T.R.I.P.E. when his adopted daughter decided to&nbsp;
become a new Star-Spangled Kid. While his new life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.840
came with plenty of challenges, he's probably&nbsp;
glad he didn't have to die in Ancient Egypt.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.920
While most people accept that Courtney Whitmore&nbsp;
is a smart and capable young woman eager to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.240
others embrace the best sides of themselves,&nbsp;
she didn't start out that way. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.720
in her early appearances, she came across as&nbsp;
an entitled brat who gets into the superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.040
life for the most selfish of reasons —&nbsp;
to screw with her step-father's life.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.560
In the original "Stars and S.T.R.I.P.E."&nbsp;
series, Courtney discovers the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.120
Star-Spangled Kid's gear in her step-father's&nbsp;
belongings and uses it to create her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.440
version of the Star-Spangled Kid's costume&nbsp;
and promptly starts getting into trouble.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.760
Courtney even attempts to use her knowledge&nbsp;
of Dugan's superhero past to get her mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.920
to leave him. Luckily, Dugan and&nbsp;
Courtney gradually form a closer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.320
relationship and Courtney's experiences&nbsp;
as Stargirl help her mature. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.480
she admits that she became a superhero for&nbsp;
the wrong reasons, and that her stepfather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.320
was born with a moral compass that she&nbsp;
had to learn how to develop for herself.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.560
Superheroes need to know how to take&nbsp;
care of themselves on the battlefield.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:55.520
This is particularly true of young superheroes&nbsp;
whose inexperience might get them killed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.680
However, Courtney Whitmore often displays&nbsp;
such a violent streak in her fights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.120
that readers are left feeling&nbsp;
almost sorry for her enemies.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.520
In "Stars and S.T.R.I.P.E." #1, Courtney&nbsp;
meets a school bully on the first day at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.120
her new high school and decides to kick him&nbsp;
in the face when he starts mouthing off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.040
Another issue actually shows Courtney kicking&nbsp;
a bad guy in the crotch during a battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.800
and relishing the opportunity to&nbsp;
use such dirty fighting tactics.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.760
To be fair, many of the foes Stargirl faces&nbsp;
off against are homicidal and Courtney probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:28.960
does need to use such extreme force in certain&nbsp;
fights. Still, her hair-trigger temper does drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:34.400
her to fight nastily in her early appearances,&nbsp;
making her seem like a super-powered delinquent.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.760
"Hey! Somebody's messing with your car!"

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.600
Family relationships can be tough for&nbsp;
superheroes, and Stargirl is no exception.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.800
In fact, Courtney Whitmore's birth father Sam&nbsp;
Kurtis just gets worse in each of his appearances.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.120
In a scene from "Stars and S.T.R.I.P.E."&nbsp;
#14 that was adapted for the TV show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:02.000
Sam shows up at Courtney's house on her&nbsp;
birthday and cons her out of a valuable locket,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.880
claiming he needs to help a non-existent&nbsp;
brother. While Courtney sees through the con,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.360
she hands over the locket anyway,&nbsp;
crushed by her dad's selfish cruelty.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.440
Later, Courtney discovers Sam has joined&nbsp;
the supervillain group the Royal Flush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.840
Gang under the alias "Two of Clubs."&nbsp;
During the "Infinite Crisis" storyline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.520
she's informed that Sam is dead, and&nbsp;
decides she doesn't want to waste her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.400
time hating a dead man who never reformed.&nbsp;
Instead, she accepts that Pat Dugan is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.400
real father figure in her life and&nbsp;
chooses to identify as his daughter.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.760
Courtney Whitmore met her original&nbsp;
arch-nemesis Cindy Burman, aka Shiv,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.720
in high school during the "Stars&nbsp;
and S.T.R.I.P.E." series. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.680
Cindy was the captain of the cheerleading squad&nbsp;
and a variation of the popular "mean girl" trope.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.560
Sounds like a fun way to explore high school&nbsp;
rivalries in a superhero setting, right?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.440
Well ... not so much. Turns out, Cindy was&nbsp;
the daughter of the Dragon King, a crime boss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.480
who tortured and experimented on her to make&nbsp;
her a living weapon. Despite Cindy's pleas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:06.320
the Dragon King regularly had cybernetic implants&nbsp;
installed in her — often without any anesthesia.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.400
Choosing to focus all of her anger and pain&nbsp;
on Courtney, Cindy attacked her superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.920
counterpart with a homicidal rage born from&nbsp;
a life of constant abuse. Her tragic story is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:20.640
so intriguing that the "Stargirl" television&nbsp;
series made it a major plotline in Season 1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.160
As portrayed by Meg DeLacy, Cindy/Shiv&nbsp;
is frightening and truly abhorrent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.960
but you can't help feeling&nbsp;
sorry for her at the same time.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.840
Superheroes and supervillains tend&nbsp;
to be connected by shared tragedy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.160
and these two are no different. In "Stars&nbsp;
and S.T.R.I.P.E." issues 12 and 13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:43.040
the Dragon King used mind-control to turn&nbsp;
the youth of Blue Valley against the adults.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.680
The brainwashing even worked on Courtney until she&nbsp;
managed to shake off its effects — distracting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.440
Dragon King long enough for the superhero&nbsp;
Shining Knight to battle the villain.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.000
During the fight, the Dragon King fell off&nbsp;
his flying dragon and died in an explosion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.760
Shiv — who was still obsessed with making&nbsp;
her father "proud" — blamed Courtney for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.240
the Dragon King's death and swore to kill&nbsp;
Courtney and everyone she cared about.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.880
Although Courtney's actions were only indirectly&nbsp;
responsible for the Dragon King's fall — Shiv's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.520
interpretation of the events earned the future&nbsp;
Stargirl an arch enemy. Ironically, in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:18.240
"Stargirl" TV series, Cindy stabs her father&nbsp;
in the back in retaliation for locking her up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.520
Nevertheless, she continues to see Stargirl as&nbsp;
her enemy and continues looking to take her down.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.400
The path of true love never runs smoothly&nbsp;
for superheroes — and that's definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.200
true for Stargirl, who found herself falling&nbsp;
for Billy Batson, a sixteen-year-old boy who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.600
worked alongside her with the Justice Society&nbsp;
of America. Nothing wrong with that, right?

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:44.320
“No. Way.”

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:47.680
Well ... not quite. As fans&nbsp;
of the movie "Shazam!" know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:52.640
Billy Batson is the teenage alter-ego of&nbsp;
the superhero Shazam, or Captain Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.800
as he was known at the time, who looks like&nbsp;
he's in his late twenties or early thirties.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.560
This made it look like Captain Marvel was&nbsp;
flirting with an underage girl when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:04.480
were hanging out with the Justice Society of&nbsp;
America. Although the two only actually dated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.960
when Billy was in his teenage form, the rest of&nbsp;
the JSA, who were unaware of Captain Marvel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:13.280
true identity, called him out on the seemingly&nbsp;
inappropriate nature of their relationship.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.880
Stargirl's first major romance might have been&nbsp;
rough, but her second was downright tragic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:24.000
Following Billy Batson's departure, Courtney found&nbsp;
herself developing feelings for Albert Rothstein,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.760
aka Atom Smasher. Al eventually reciprocated, but&nbsp;
he later fell under the influence of Black Adam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.200
who convinced him to invade the&nbsp;
oppressed country of Khandaq&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.680
and kill it's dictator president, putting&nbsp;
him in direct conflict with the JSA.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:42.880
In the ensuing battle, Al sacrifices himself&nbsp;
to save the people of Khandaq from the Spectre,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:47.280
but a distraught Black Adam is able to&nbsp;
revive him almost immediately. Back home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:50.160
Al is put on trial for his&nbsp;
actions and pleads guilty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.480
but Courtney, never one to give up, promises&nbsp;
she'll be there for him when he gets out.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.800
Making matters more difficult, there's an actual&nbsp;
age difference between Courtney and Albert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.400
although that doesn't seem to matter in&nbsp;
a possible future where an adult Courtney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:07.680
is married to Albert. Audiences can also look&nbsp;
forward to seeing Noah Centineo play Atom Smasher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:13.040
in the 2022 "Black Adam" movie alongside Dwayne&nbsp;
"The Rock" Johnson as Black Adam ... although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.880
considering their comic book history, this&nbsp;
might not be so great for Atom Smasher.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:22.800
At the core of Stargirl's appeal is her amazing&nbsp;
family dynamic. Few sidekicks are older than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:26.880
the main hero, but S.T.R.I.P.E.'s relationship&nbsp;
with Stargirl is made special by the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:31.840
Pat Dugan is Courtney's stepfather and became&nbsp;
a superhero to support and look out for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:36.800
In fact, Courtney regularly sees her family as the&nbsp;
inspiration for her superhero activities ... which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.440
is why it was so traumatizing for her to&nbsp;
see them all murdered before her eyes.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:45.760
This happened in "JSA" #68 when the&nbsp;
Red Morgue went back in time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.360
slaughtered Courtney's entire family&nbsp;
as they were all having breakfast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.200
Luckily, Time Master Rip Hunter&nbsp;
arrived soon after to save Courtney.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:57.920
Rip helped assemble a team of JSA members to&nbsp;
travel to different points in time to erase the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.600
events leading up to the Dugan-Whitmore&nbsp;
family's murder and set things right.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.480
Saving the universe and leading a double life&nbsp;
can be tough on a person's mental health,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.560
but one adventure saw Stargirl&nbsp;
literally land in an insane asylum.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:13.280
During the events of the "Black&nbsp;
Vengeance" JSA storyline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:17.360
Courtney traveled back in time to erase&nbsp;
the events leading to her family's murder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.640
Courtney's mission was to travel to the year 1951&nbsp;
and recruit Ted Knight, the original Starman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.640
but unfortunately he was committed to&nbsp;
an insane asylum at that point in time.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:31.680
Before she could convince him that she wasn't a&nbsp;
drug-induced hallucination, the asylum orderlies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:36.960
spotted her and drugged her. Courtney was strapped&nbsp;
into a straitjacket and tossed into a padded cell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.200
Luckily, by "JSA" #70, Courtney's&nbsp;
time-traveling sister Patricia managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.200
to free her. While her time as a mental&nbsp;
patient was brief, it likely remains a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.800
dark spot in Courtney's memory of how&nbsp;
superheroes are viewed by some people.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.280
Despite the fact that she wears a mask, a&nbsp;
lot of people know that Courtney Whitmore and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.760
Stargirl are one and the same. Her family,&nbsp;
the entire Justice Society of America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.200
and even several of her villains&nbsp;
know Stargirl's true identity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.360
As it turns out, a lot of this is due to&nbsp;
Courtney's carelessness — she once exposed her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.160
secret identity to her friend Mary on the night&nbsp;
of her first adventure as the Star-Spangled Kid.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.680
Sometimes, the fact that practically&nbsp;
everyone knows Courtney is Stargirl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:18.320
is used for comedic effect — like when the JSA&nbsp;
visits Courtney during a dentist's appointment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:22.720
Other times, however, writers remind readers that&nbsp;
the reason for the secret identity was so villains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.040
wouldn't come after the hero's loved ones ...&nbsp;
something that tragically happens to Stargirl.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.280
"I put all of us in so much danger,&nbsp;
because I believed in some fairy tale."

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.400
In "Justice League of America" issues 10&nbsp;
through 12, Courtney gets on the supervillain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.960
Shadow Thief's radar. A few issues later,&nbsp;
Shadow Thief tracks down Courtney's family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:47.520
wounds her mom, and kills her little brother.&nbsp;
Although the experience helps motivate Courtney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:52.480
to be a better superhero, the cost is&nbsp;
extremely high ... and extremely dark.

